<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?><parameters><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>S4_HOSTNAME</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>true</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>Base address of your SAP S/4HANA system, including the protocol — for example https://my123456-api.s4hana.cloud.sap. Must start with https://; the flow refuses every request against a plain http:// address so that credentials are never sent unencrypted. The one exception is a system behind an SAP Cloud Connector (proxy type sapcc): there, enter the virtual host defined in the Cloud Connector, written with http:// — for example http://s4hana.virtual:44300. Nothing travels unencrypted, the Cloud Connector's tunnel does the encrypting.</description>
    <additionalMetadata/>
  </parameter><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>S4_AUTH_METHOD</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>true</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>How this flow signs in to SAP S/4HANA; choose one of the entries the screen offers. OAuth2 Client Credentials, the shipped default, is the method of a communication arrangement on SAP S/4HANA Cloud that issues a client ID and secret. Basic is a user name and a password, the method for an on-premise or private-edition system and for a system behind an SAP Cloud Connector. Client Certificate signs in with a key pair from this tenant's keystore. The security material named in S4_CREDENTIAL_ALIAS, or the key pair named in S4_PRIVATE_KEY_ALIAS, must be of the matching type.</description>
    <additionalMetadata>
      <isCombobox>true</isCombobox>
    </additionalMetadata>
  </parameter><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>S4_CREDENTIAL_ALIAS</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>true</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>Name of the security material in this tenant that holds the sign-in details for SAP S/4HANA. Create it under Monitor, Manage Security, Security Material. The material's type must match S4_AUTH_METHOD: OAuth2 Client Credentials for the shipped default, User Credentials for Basic. Not used with Client Certificate. On SAP S/4HANA Cloud the user name it holds also decides which communication arrangements count as this connection's own.</description>
    <additionalMetadata/>
  </parameter><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>S4_PRIVATE_KEY_ALIAS</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>false</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>Alias of the key pair in this tenant's keystore (Monitor, Manage Security, Keystore) that identifies this tenant to SAP S/4HANA when S4_AUTH_METHOD is Client Certificate. Leave empty for the other methods.</description>
    <additionalMetadata/>
  </parameter><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>HTTP_TIMEOUT_MS</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>false</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>How long a single call to SAP S/4HANA may take before it is abandoned, in milliseconds, 1 or more. The flow makes one attempt per call and answers 504 when a call passes this; one request for the list makes up to six calls in sequence plus the verification calls bounded by CATALOG_VERIFY_LIMIT, so keep the value well below a sixth of the calling application's own timeout. Keboola's SAP OData component waits 60 seconds unless its own timeout setting says otherwise.</description>
    <additionalMetadata/>
  </parameter><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>S4_PROXY_TYPE</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>false</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>How this tenant reaches your SAP S/4HANA system. Use default when the system is reachable over the internet, or sapcc when it sits behind an SAP Cloud Connector. Where the screen offers a list, these are its entries Internet and On-Premise.</description>
    <additionalMetadata/>
  </parameter><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>S4_CC_LOCATION_ID</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>false</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>Location identifier of the SAP Cloud Connector to use. Leave empty unless you run more than one Cloud Connector against this tenant and set the proxy type to sapcc.</description>
    <additionalMetadata/>
  </parameter><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>AIR_KEY</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>false</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>Integration key issued by SAP for this package, sent with every call so SAP can recognise the integration. Leave empty unless the documentation of this package gives you a key.</description>
    <additionalMetadata/>
  </parameter><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>AIR_HEADER_NAME</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>false</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>Name of the request header the integration key is sent in, as stated in the instructions SAP supplies with the key. Nothing is sent unless both this and the key are filled in.</description>
    <additionalMetadata/>
  </parameter><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>S4_SAP_CLIENT</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>false</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>Client number of the SAP system to sign in to, for example 100. Needed only on an on-premise or private-edition system with more than one client; leave empty for SAP S/4HANA Cloud and for single-client systems. When set it is sent as sap-client with every call.</description>
    <additionalMetadata/>
  </parameter><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>SENDER_ROLE</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>true</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>User role a caller must hold to reach this endpoint; the platform checks it before the flow runs and answers 403 without a log entry when it is missing. ESBMessaging.send, the shipped value, is held by every integration client of this tenant. To open the endpoint to Keboola alone, create a role of your own under Monitor, Manage Security, User Roles, grant it to the service instance whose key Keboola uses, and name it here.</description>
    <additionalMetadata/>
  </parameter><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>CATALOG_SOURCE</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>false</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>Where the list of services is read from. One of three values:
- auto: the communication arrangements of SAP S/4HANA Cloud first (communication scenario SAP_COM_0A07, the arrangements of this connection's user); when the system has none, as an on-premise or private-edition system has not, the system's own Gateway catalogues (OData V2 and V4).
- arrangements: the communication arrangements only.
- gateway: the Gateway catalogues only.</description>
    <additionalMetadata/>
  </parameter><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>CATALOG_VIEW</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>false</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>Which services the list shows when it is read from the Gateway catalogues. One of three values:
- interfaces: services meant to be read by other systems (what SAP classifies as a web API, services you built yourself, anything named API_, released OData V4 services).
- extended: everything except the backends of Fiori apps and OData V4 views that are neither released nor your own (a name that starts with Z or Y).
- all: everything the catalogues list, including Fiori app backends and raw CDS views.
A list read from the communication arrangements is the same in all three. A support call can override the value with ?include= on the address.</description>
    <additionalMetadata/>
  </parameter><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>CATALOG_RESOLVE_V4</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>false</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>How an OData V4 service of a communication arrangement gets its address, which the arrangement does not carry. One of three values:
- lookup+verify: the address comes from the value mapping KeboolaServiceAddresses of this package; a service the mapping does not know is tried at up to four addresses built from its name, one small request each to the service's own document, and listed at the first one that answers.
- lookup: the value mapping only; a service it does not know is left out.
- off: no OData V4 service of an arrangement is listed.
Services left out are counted in the response header X-Keboola-Catalog-Unlisted and named in the run's log property CatalogUnlistedNames; add them to the value mapping.</description>
    <additionalMetadata/>
  </parameter><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>CATALOG_VERIFY_LIMIT</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>false</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>How many of the small requests that try an address for an unknown OData V4 service one request for the list may make in all, 0 to 200; the services beyond the limit are left out and named as unlisted. Each request takes about a tenth of a second on SAP S/4HANA Cloud. 0 switches the requests off.</description>
    <additionalMetadata/>
  </parameter><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>CATALOG_DIAGNOSTICS</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>false</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>Whether a caller may ask for the run's diagnostics with ?debug=1 on the address: the sources read, their answers and the services left out. true or false. Leave false unless support asks for it: the diagnostics name the system's answers, and every client holding the endpoint's role can read them.</description>
    <additionalMetadata/>
  </parameter><param_references><reference attribute_category="Receiver" attribute_id="ctype::AdapterVariant/cname::HTTP/tp::HTTP/mp::None/direction::Receiver/version::1.17.0/attrId::httpAddressWithoutQuery" attribute_uilabel="Address" param_key="S4_HOSTNAME"/><reference attribute_category="FlowElement" attribute_id="ctype::FlowstepVariant/cname::Enricher/version::1.6.3/attrId::propertyTable" attribute_uilabel="Exchange Property" param_key="S4_HOSTNAME"/><reference attribute_category="Receiver" attribute_id="ctype::AdapterVariant/cname::HTTP/tp::HTTP/mp::None/direction::Receiver/version::1.17.0/attrId::authenticationMethod" attribute_uilabel="Authentication" param_key="S4_AUTH_METHOD"/><reference attribute_category="Receiver" attribute_id="ctype::AdapterVariant/cname::HTTP/tp::HTTP/mp::None/direction::Receiver/version::1.17.0/attrId::credentialName" attribute_uilabel="Credential Name" param_key="S4_CREDENTIAL_ALIAS"/><reference attribute_category="FlowElement" attribute_id="ctype::FlowstepVariant/cname::Enricher/version::1.6.3/attrId::propertyTable" attribute_uilabel="Exchange Property" param_key="S4_CREDENTIAL_ALIAS"/><reference attribute_category="Receiver" attribute_id="ctype::AdapterVariant/cname::HTTP/tp::HTTP/mp::None/direction::Receiver/version::1.17.0/attrId::privateKeyAlias" attribute_uilabel="Private Key Alias" param_key="S4_PRIVATE_KEY_ALIAS"/><reference attribute_category="Receiver" attribute_id="ctype::AdapterVariant/cname::HTTP/tp::HTTP/mp::None/direction::Receiver/version::1.17.0/attrId::httpRequestTimeout" attribute_uilabel="Timeout (in ms)" param_key="HTTP_TIMEOUT_MS"/><reference attribute_category="FlowElement" attribute_id="ctype::FlowstepVariant/cname::Enricher/version::1.6.3/attrId::propertyTable" attribute_uilabel="Exchange Property" param_key="HTTP_TIMEOUT_MS"/><reference attribute_category="Receiver" attribute_id="ctype::AdapterVariant/cname::HTTP/tp::HTTP/mp::None/direction::Receiver/version::1.17.0/attrId::proxyType" attribute_uilabel="Proxy Type" param_key="S4_PROXY_TYPE"/><reference attribute_category="FlowElement" attribute_id="ctype::FlowstepVariant/cname::Enricher/version::1.6.3/attrId::propertyTable" attribute_uilabel="Exchange Property" param_key="S4_PROXY_TYPE"/><reference attribute_category="Receiver" attribute_id="ctype::AdapterVariant/cname::HTTP/tp::HTTP/mp::None/direction::Receiver/version::1.17.0/attrId::locationID" attribute_uilabel="Location ID" param_key="S4_CC_LOCATION_ID"/><reference attribute_category="FlowElement" attribute_id="ctype::FlowstepVariant/cname::Enricher/version::1.6.3/attrId::propertyTable" attribute_uilabel="Exchange Property" param_key="S4_CC_LOCATION_ID"/><reference attribute_category="FlowElement" attribute_id="ctype::FlowstepVariant/cname::Enricher/version::1.6.3/attrId::propertyTable" attribute_uilabel="Exchange Property" param_key="AIR_KEY"/><reference attribute_category="FlowElement" attribute_id="ctype::FlowstepVariant/cname::Enricher/version::1.6.3/attrId::propertyTable" attribute_uilabel="Exchange Property" param_key="AIR_HEADER_NAME"/><reference attribute_category="FlowElement" attribute_id="ctype::FlowstepVariant/cname::Enricher/version::1.6.3/attrId::propertyTable" attribute_uilabel="Exchange Property" param_key="S4_SAP_CLIENT"/><reference attribute_category="Sender" attribute_id="ctype::AdapterVariant/cname::HTTPS/tp::HTTPS/mp::None/direction::Sender/version::1.5.2/attrId::userRole" attribute_uilabel="User Role" param_key="SENDER_ROLE"/><reference attribute_category="FlowElement" attribute_id="ctype::FlowstepVariant/cname::Enricher/version::1.6.3/attrId::propertyTable" attribute_uilabel="Exchange Property" param_key="CATALOG_SOURCE"/><reference attribute_category="FlowElement" attribute_id="ctype::FlowstepVariant/cname::Enricher/version::1.6.3/attrId::propertyTable" attribute_uilabel="Exchange Property" param_key="CATALOG_VIEW"/><reference attribute_category="FlowElement" attribute_id="ctype::FlowstepVariant/cname::Enricher/version::1.6.3/attrId::propertyTable" attribute_uilabel="Exchange Property" param_key="CATALOG_RESOLVE_V4"/><reference attribute_category="FlowElement" attribute_id="ctype::FlowstepVariant/cname::Enricher/version::1.6.3/attrId::propertyTable" attribute_uilabel="Exchange Property" param_key="CATALOG_VERIFY_LIMIT"/><reference attribute_category="FlowElement" attribute_id="ctype::FlowstepVariant/cname::Enricher/version::1.6.3/attrId::propertyTable" attribute_uilabel="Exchange Property" param_key="CATALOG_DIAGNOSTICS"/></param_references></parameters>